  "id": "14-trace-inventory-map-v2",
  "title": "Where every trace lives · 2026-11-05",
  "description": "Inventory of every agent trace source on Ford's machines on 2026-11-05, with sizes, and the planned path each takes to nas-01. Nothing moves today.\n\n**Layout (left → right):** source machines (command-center with its two writer groups, dev-01 and recording-01 stacked below it; Daytona sandboxes sit above services-01 and feed trace-ingest from the top) → services-01 (Collectors: Backfill job, trace-ingest, Raw feed spool, ClickHouse; Local trace stores in two columns below, feeding up into the collectors) → nas-01 destination folders. The key and the nas-01 paths note sit top-right, above the services-01 → nas-01 band.\n\n**Frame colours:** violet = source machine; teal = services-01 (Mac mini), the only NAS writer; orange = its Collectors group; pink = its local trace stores; blue = nas-01, unreachable today.\n\n**Wire key:** violet = one-time backfill via the Backfill job; green = live collection via trace-ingest and the Raw feed spool; pink dashed = waits on the Archon fork; gray = Token Gateway nightly sqlite copy. Every wire into nas-01 starts on services-01.\n\n**Node key:** blue = trace source; orange = store at risk now (T3 span logs on dev-01 and recording-01, Token Gateway, Budget kernel + Pi, T3 logs + sessions); yellow key glyph = codex-lb proxy store, which holds account tokens; teal = services-01 mover; green = nas-01 copy.",
